===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm|stemmen}}, a borrowing from {{der|en|non|stemma|t=to stop, stem, dam}} (whence {{cog|da|stemme}}/{{m|da|stæmme||to stem, dam up}}), from {{der|en|gem-pro|*stammijaną}}. Cognate with {{cog|de|stemmen}}, {{cog|dum|stemmen}}, {{m|dum|stempen}}. Compare {{m|en|stammer}}.

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[stop]], hinder (for instance, a river or blood).
#: ''to '''stem''' a tide''
#* {{RQ:Denham Poems
|poem=The Destruction of Troy|passage=[They] '''stem''' the flood with their erected breasts.}}
#* {{RQ:Pope Essay on Criticism|passage='''Stemm'd''' the wild torrent of a barbarous age.}}
# {{lb|en|skiing}} To move the feet apart and point the tips of the skis inward in order to slow down the speed or to facilitate a turn.
# In rock climbing, to use a stance with the feet spread apart, bracing them in opposite directions against the two walls of a chimney or dihedral.

